1. Ensure path resolution helpers handle non-string or null/undefined inputs gracefully (e.g., by returning null) to allow the application to fail closed or log diagnostics instead of throwing a TypeError and crashing.
2. When constructing file or artifact paths using helper functions, validate that all path components (such as IDs and suffixes) are non-empty strings, returning null if any required component is missing or invalid to prevent generating paths with literal 'null' or 'undefined' substrings.
</details>

